 among the first users  and rumors have it that the first users  used their  waiting time while the samples were  exposed to  play squash in empty hutches and use the  smooth concrete floors  for rollerblading i would not know  anything about these rumors  so i will deny all all accounts of this  that's all i'll say about it so now  remember what the  the result that we get from diffraction  experiments  is not the structure itself it is  actually the electron density  the electron density without a model  built into it tells us nothing  the electron dens so so then i had to  sit for about a year in a dark room  painstakingly and manually building  a three-dimensional structure into this  model now this was  really really difficult because we had  no idea where to start we had no idea  what the secondary structure of these  proteins was  we had no idea where the dna was this is  the raw data that we had and so this is  like a big three-dimensional puzzle  and only when all the parts are fitted  correctly you can account for all the  electron density  and so this is what the final product  then would look like  and this this required as i said about  one year of work  in a dark room uh in front of a computer  monitor  not a very social experience here's a  detailed  a detailed view of the same density  and you can see that now we can actually  obtain the orientation of the  main chain and of the side chains of the  protein and this allowed us  to really uh to to describe  how the dna is held so tightly by the  histones how the histones interact with  each other  and this gives that give rise to this  iconic picture here of the  final nucleosome structure two different  orientation that now graces mouse pads  and textbooks and t-shirts  and it's just generally very very pretty  to look  at like all scientific endeavors  uh this particular uh  project uh took very many years  and it was a huge group effort and  couldn't have been done without my  colleagues at the eth  zurich with the guidance of tim richmond  you
 

